Do not bring a hidden workspace back when a layer surface gives up focus

When a layer surface that held the keyboard closes, refocusLastWindow gives
focus back to the last focused window. Its first branch does that only if the
window's workspace is visible, but the fallback, taken when the pointer is
over an overlay or top layer surface that cannot take the keyboard, focused
the window whatever its workspace. Focusing a window on a hidden workspace
switches to that workspace, so with focus left on a window of a hidden
special workspace, closing a bar popup with the pointer over the bar showed
the special workspace again.

Give the fallback the same visibility check as the branch above it.

Not yet upstream.

--- a/src/managers/input/InputManager.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/input/InputManager.cpp
@@ -1893,8 +1893,10 @@
         // otherwise fall back to a normal refocus.
 
         if (foundSurface && !foundSurface->m_hlSurface->keyboardFocusable()) {
+            // not a window on a hidden workspace: focusing it would switch to that workspace
             const auto PLASTWINDOW = Desktop::focusState()->window();
-            Desktop::focusState()->fullWindowFocus(PLASTWINDOW, Desktop::FOCUS_REASON_FFM);
+            if (!PLASTWINDOW || (PLASTWINDOW->m_workspace && PLASTWINDOW->m_workspace->isVisibleNotCovered()))
+                Desktop::focusState()->fullWindowFocus(PLASTWINDOW, Desktop::FOCUS_REASON_FFM);
         }
 
         refocus();
